- * second under Box86, on a set of resources that barely changes between draws;
- * these access_time writes are still emulated x86 work.
- *
- * The question this answers is only "how many access_time marks, on how many
- * distinct resources". A simple producer-side dedup is NOT safe: a later draw
- * advances the queue head, so leaving an older access_time can let destruction
- * pass the later packet. Any optimization here needs an explicit lifetime hold
- * released by the consumer; this counter alone does not authorize one.
- *
- *   MGS2_WINED3D_REFSTATS=1   counters only, one line per second
